  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'all the operating systems that Qt supports' lacks concrete scope — Qt’s supported OS list evolves across versions (e.g., Qt 5.15 vs Qt 6.5), and 'supports' is undefined (build-time? runtime? official binaries only?). Users cannot reliably interpret what 'all' means without version context.", "A":"'all the operating systems that Qt supports' is ambiguous because Qt’s support matrix varies by module, build configuration (e.g., no GUI on headless Linux), and target architecture; 'supports' has no normative definition in this requirement, enabling multiple incompatible interpretations.", "C":"The statement is likely correct *in intent*, as cross-platform compatibility is a core Qt goal, but correctness cannot be assessed without binding to a specific Qt version and supported platform list — no factual error is evident, yet verifiability failure undermines confidence in correctness.", "V":"No testable criterion is provided: there is no defined list of OS names, versions, or configurations; no pass/fail condition (e.g., 'must launch and respond to user input on each OS'); 'run' is undefined (startup only? full functionality? no crash within 5s?) — thus fundamentally unverifiable."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Specify Qt version and enumerate exact OS targets (e.g., 'Qt 6.7 LTS, running on Ubuntu 22.04 LTS x86_64, Windows 10 22H2 x64, and macOS 13.6 Ventura ARM64').", "A":"Replace 'all the operating systems that Qt supports' with a version-bound, enumerated list of OS-target-arch triples defined in the project’s approved platform matrix.", "C":"Keep unchanged — but only if paired with an authoritative, version-locked platform matrix referenced elsewhere; standalone, it remains weakly correct.", "V":"Must be rewritten to name specific OS-target-arch combinations and define 'run' as: 'successfully initialize, enter main event loop, and accept user input within 3 seconds without termination or unhandled exception.'"},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"It must run with all the operating systems that Qt supports.","rewrite":"The software shall run on the following Qt 6.7.2-supported platforms: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (x86_64), Windows 10 version 22H2 (x64), and macOS 13.6 Ventura (ARM64)."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"all the operating systems that Qt supports","rewrite":"Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (x86_64), Windows 10 version 22H2 (x64), and macOS 13.6 Ventura (ARM64), as validated against Qt 6.7.2 official binary distributions."},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"It must run with all the operating systems that Qt supports.","rewrite":"On each of the specified platforms, the application shall start, reach the Qt event loop, and accept keyboard/mouse input within 3 seconds of launch without crashing, hanging, or throwing unhandled exceptions."}
  ]
}
